# Guide

Split a guide into chapters only when each chapter answers a different task and stands alone for someone who arrives directly. If readers need the whole procedure at once, use a [detailed guide](detailed-guide.html) with a contents list. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it when sections are useful independently. A companion installation guide might separate preparation, installation and verification.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep one title style and one chapter navigation. Mark the current chapter without a self-link. Give previous and next links the chapter names ([WG-083](../../content/writing-guidelines/add-links.html#wg-083)). Offer a combined print view only if it holds the whole guide. Keep terminology and version requirements the same across chapters.

## Home Assistant boundary

A run of guide pages is not a wizard and must not save progress silently. Do not leave a necessary prerequisite on an earlier page that a direct visitor may never see ([WG-051](../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html#wg-051)). The examples link to real sections, not invented URLs.

